\ Bounded-memory regression for executed closure bodies.
\
\ Executing a curry or compose product used to leave a permanent entry in the
\ body-keyed resolution maps, keyed by a body address the closure frees on
\ release. The loop words build one closure per iteration, so every loop below
\ `times` grew memory linearly with its iteration count and exhausted the 4 MB
\ cap set in the `.flags` sidecar partway through. A closure-owned body now
\ never enters the maps, so all three probes stay flat.

50000 [ 1 [ drop ] curry call ] times

0 [ 1 + dup 50000 < ] loop drop

50000 [ dup 0 > ] [ 1 - ] while drop

"flat" print-line
